It&#39;s a half baked beta all the time.

And the answer to all the things it can&#39;t do: &#39;just go to the web.&#39;

Except I installed the app, so opening cal.goog in the browser _forces_ me into the app.

Love the contents of this app greatly but I&#39;m OCD enough to really get bothered when I see the app name under it as &#34;GoogleCalendar&#34; 

No space. 

Why, god? WHY?

Updated! Thank you for adding widgets. Absolutely the best!

//

&#34;Can&#39;t believe there&#39;s still no widget. Especially after iOS 10 came out. I could completely delete Apple&#39;s calendar app if you add in a widget.&#34;

Overall the best calendar app I&#39;ve used. Very intuitive and syncs well with other Google suite products. Two suggestions: 
1) As others noted, it&#39;d be great if the icon indicated the actual date, not default &#34;31&#34; 
2) The app name was shortened so it&#39;s not cut off to &#34;Google Cal...&#34; by default on iPhone.

There is a pop up notification reminder that says the word &#34;NOW&#34; (upper right) even though my appointment is 2 hours from &#39;NOW&#39;. The notification makes my heart skip a beat whenever it pops up. Please delete that word and just have the title and maybe include the actual time of the appointment as the pop up notification. Anything but the word &#34;NOW&#34; 

I would appreciate the actual date displayed as the thumbnail icon.

Thank you.

Google is my personal calendar of choice, and it looks/functions great on the desktop website. However, this app is terrible by comparison! 

No month view is a deal-breaker. Not very user friendly, stupidly over simplified interface makes it impossible to get any real events entered in without thinking &#34;wow this app is useless...&#34;

Save yourself the trouble and download Calendars 5 instead, it&#39;s a FAR SUPERIOR app.
